# The same drawing, where each place is pushed onto a list the body changes. A loop is a step: it takes what it goes
# over and gives each element under the name it binds, so the node and the touch are values the body makes, `Node·n`
# from the graph and `Touch·t` from the node, and `t.drawn()` on the loop's `t` is `Touch.drawn`, as on the clean side's
# element. `out.push(..)` makes the list anew from the Where it is handed; `out: Where[]` holds Wheres, as `vec![]`
# gathering them does in Rust, and starts as `[]`, a literal of a type of the code's, which the body makes itself where it
# binds the name (#237). The push in the loop takes that list, as a change after the binding does (#366), and the body
# gives back what the push made. The plan is the Rust method pair's (`../rust-method/shortcut.plan`) but for the list it
# starts from: Rust's `vec![]` writes no type, so there the push takes no list.

route drawing.drawn
step drawn/for n of g.nodes
step drawn/for t of n.touches
step drawn/Touch.drawn
step drawn/Touch.drawn/Where()
step drawn/push                                                # `out.push(t.drawn())`

line entry > drawn call
line Graph·g > drawn value                                    # the route's own parameter, from its start
line Graph·g > drawn/for n of g.nodes value
line drawn/for n of g.nodes > Node·n@drawn/for n of g.nodes value
line Node·n@drawn/for n of g.nodes > drawn/for t of n.touches value
line drawn/for t of n.touches > Touch·t@drawn/for t of n.touches value
line Touch·t@drawn/for t of n.touches > drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() value   # `this.op`
line drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() > Where@drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() value
line Where@drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() > drawn/Touch.drawn value
line drawn/Touch.drawn > Where@drawn/Touch.drawn value
line Where@drawn/Touch.drawn > drawn/push value
line Where·out@drawn/~out > drawn/push value                  # `const out: Where[] = []`, the body's own list
line drawn/push > Where·out@drawn/push value
line Where·out@drawn/push > drawn value                       # given back
line drawn > Where@drawn value                                # and given, at the route's moment

home Graph·g drawn
home Where@drawn drawn
home Node·n@drawn/for n of g.nodes drawn
home Touch·t@drawn/for t of n.touches drawn
home Where@drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() drawn/Touch.drawn
home Where@drawn/Touch.drawn drawn
home Where·out@drawn/~out drawn
home Where·out@drawn/push drawn

side entry left
